# clang-tidy overrides for tests/ ONLY. Inherits the repo-root .clang-tidy and
# subtracts exactly one check. Library code under src/ and include/ keeps the
# full curated set — nothing here weakens the gate where it catches real bugs.
#
# -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access
#   The analyzer cannot see through this suite's own assertion macro. Every test
#   here is a `bool` function and ASSERT_TRUE is (test_main.cpp:36):
#
#       #define ASSERT_TRUE(x) do { if (!(x)) { ...; return false; } } while (0)
#
#   so `ASSERT_TRUE(opt.has_value());` genuinely guards the `opt.value()` on the
#   next line — the function has already returned if the optional was empty.
#   clang-tidy's dataflow model does not treat the macro's `return false` as a
#   narrowing of the optional's state, so it reports every such access as
#   unchecked.
#
#   Verified before disabling, NOT assumed: all 13 findings in the 2026-07-30 CI
#   run (test_agent.cpp:263, test_config_loader.cpp:57, and 11 in
#   test_relay_states_mock.cpp) were each checked against their enclosing TEST
#   block. Every one has an `ASSERT_TRUE(...has_value())` on the immediately
#   preceding line, or a single guard covering its small block. ZERO were real
#   unchecked accesses.
#
#   The alternatives are all worse: `*opt` instead of `.value()` hides the throw
#   without adding a check; `if (!opt) return false;` duplicates the assertion and
#   drops the failure message naming the expectation; per-line NOLINT on 13 sites
#   is noise that every newly-added assertion re-earns. Per RULES.md §3, a check
#   that fails correct, wire-neutral code is mis-scoped for that context — fix the
#   scope, not the code.
#
#   Scoped to tests/ precisely so a REAL unchecked optional access in shipping
#   code still reds the LINT gate.
#   InheritParentConfig is REQUIRED. Without it a nested .clang-tidy REPLACES the
#   parent's check list rather than extending it, so this file would leave tests/
#   with "Error: no checks enabled" — every rule silently off, while appearing to
#   disable exactly one. Caught by RUNNING the gate, not by reading the config.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: '-bugprone-unchecked-optional-access'
